# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ad-hoc debug dumps at the repo root
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Redirecting a build or test run to a file at the repo root is a normal way to
# capture output, but 25 such files had accumulated untracked and would have
# shipped in a source tarball. These patterns are deliberately anchored to the
# root with a leading slash so a legitimately tracked file of the same name
# deeper in the tree is unaffected.
/dump_*.txt
/nf_*.txt
/tmp_*.txt
/stdout*.txt
/stderr*.txt
/test_err.txt
/test_out.txt
/full_test_*.txt
/llvm_out.txt
/llvm_err.txt
/build_errors.txt
/wasm_test_output.txt

# Scratch directory for one-off reproductions.
/tmp/

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local build configuration
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# .cargo/config.toml here pins a machine-specific linker (lld-link) and other
# host-tuned build settings. Committing it breaks a fresh clone on any machine
# without that toolchain, which is exactly the portability problem the release
# work is removing, so it stays local.
/.cargo/

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment / secrets
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.env
*.local

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ML models
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
models/

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CI artifacts
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/ci-artifacts/
/sqlite3.dll
/scratch_test.iris
/IRIS-Book.pdf

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
env/
.build_new_book.py


# Vendored native libraries.
#
# These were committed in the branch's first commit -- 27 files, 1.28 GB, with
# tensorflow.dll at 909 MB and torch_cpu.dll at 240 MB, both over GitHub's
# 100 MB hard limit. That made the branch unpushable, and no amount of chunking
# helps: the blobs are in the history, so every push is rejected.
#
# ML backends are resolved at runtime via dlopen (see src/runtime/
# iris_ml_dynload.h), so these belong in a local install, not in git.
*.dll
*.exe
*.lib
*.so
*.dylib
*.pdb

# Build artifacts. ~11.3 GB of these were committed and later removed, so the
# blobs stayed in history: target/ 6.6 GB, target-local-ci/ 1.6 GB,
# fuzz/target/ 841 MB, plus target-run*/ target-test*/ target_verify/ and
# vscode-iris/node_modules/. Purged from this branch's history; keep them out.
/target-*/
/target_*/
fuzz/target/
vscode-iris/node_modules/
vscode-iris/out/
